.Dd July 2, 2026
.Dt MINI-SNMPD.CONF 5
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm mini-snmpd.conf
.Nd configuration file for mini-snmpd
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is the optional configuration file for
.Xr mini-snmpd 8 ,
read at start-up and again on
.Dv SIGHUP .
The default path is
.Pa /etc/mini-snmpd.conf ,
override it with
.Fl f .
The file is only supported when
.Nm mini-snmpd
is built with libConfuse; without it all settings are given on the
command line.
.Pp
Settings combine with the command line rather than replacing it: a scalar
present in the file overrides the matching command-line option, the list
settings are appended to what
.Fl d , Fl i ,
and
.Fl T
provided, and a key left out of the file keeps its command-line value.
.Pp
The syntax is that of libConfuse: one
.Ar key No = Ar value
per line, string values in double quotes, lists as a brace-enclosed,
comma-separated set.  Anything after a
.Ql #
is a comment.
.Sh SETTINGS
.Bl -tag -width Ds
.It Ic community Ar STR
Community string, default
.Qq public .
Same as
.Fl c .
.It Ic authentication Ar true Ns | Ns Ar false
Require the community string to match, thus SNMP version 2c, default
.Ar false .
Same as
.Fl a .
.It Ic location Ar STR
.Sy sysLocation ,
default empty.  Same as
.Fl L .
.It Ic contact Ar STR
.Sy sysContact ,
default empty.  Same as
.Fl C .
.It Ic description Ar STR
.Sy sysDescr .
If unset, the
.Sy PRETTY_NAME
from
.Xr os-release 5
is used.  Same as
.Fl D .
.It Ic vendor Ar OID
.Sy sysObjectID ,
the vendor OID, default
.Li .1.3.6.1.4.1 .
Same as
.Fl V .
.It Ic timeout Ar SEC
Interval between MIB value updates, in seconds, default 1.  Same as
.Fl t .
.It Ic disk-table Ar { "DIR", ... }
Mount points to report in
.Sy UCD-SNMP-MIB::dskTable ,
default
.Ql / .
Adds to any
.Fl d .
.It Ic iface-table Ar { "IFNAME", ... }
Interfaces to report in the IF-MIB.  A trailing
.Ql +
is a prefix wildcard, iptables style, e.g.
.Ql eth+ ;
a lone
.Ql +
matches all.  With no entry, all interfaces are monitored, loopback
first.  Adds to any
.Fl i .
.It Ic trap-table Ar { "ADDR[:PORT]", ... }
SNMPv2c trap sinks, default port 162, IPv6 as
.Ql [addr]:port .
Adds to any
.Fl T .
.El
.Pp
A
.Ic custom
section serves a fixed string on any OID, e.g. to emulate the responses
of another device.  The section title is the OID, in leading-dot form:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
custom ".1.3.6.1.4.1.11.2.3.9.1.1.7.0" {
        value = "MFG:Hewlett-Packard;MDL:HP LaserJet 1020;CLS:PRINTER;"
}
.Ed
.Pp
Up to eight
.Ic custom
sections are supported; an OID already served by a built-in MIB is
rejected.
.Pp
Unless built with
.Fl -disable-ethtool ,
one or more
.Ic ethtool
sections map driver statistics onto IF-MIB counters for the matching
interfaces:
.Bd -literal -offset indent
ethtool "eth*" {
        rx_bytes      = ifInOctets
        rx_packets    = ifInUcastPkts
        tx_bytes      = ifOutOctets
        tx_packets    = ifOutUcastPkts
}
.Ed
.Pp
The section title is a shell-style glob matched against the interface
name; each key names an ethtool driver statistic and each value the
IF-MIB object it feeds.
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width /etc/mini-snmpd.conf -compact
.It Pa /etc/mini-snmpd.conf
default configuration file
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bd -literal -offset indent
community      = "public"
authentication = true
location       = "Exampleville Site 1."
contact        = "ops@example.com"
description    = "NAS monitor"
timeout        = 1
disk-table     = { "/", "/var" }
trap-table     = { "192.0.2.1", "[2001:db8::1]:1620" }
.Ed
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr mini-snmpd 8
